Lookup the meaning of the word "veridical". {lo} is and /always has been/
veridical- it must and can only be used for things which /actually are/
what you're describing them as. {le} is and /always has been/ non-veridical=
.

xorlo did not change the meaning of {lo} or {le}, it just changed how
quantification works.


